  "notes": [
    "Source: raw HTML of https://claycorp.com/ fetched 2026-10-09 with curl -sL and a desktop Chrome User-Agent (HTTP 200, 177,596 bytes). Primary tree parsed from <nav class=\"nmcnav_wrap\" id=\"nmcnav_wrap\" aria-label=\"Site Navigation\"> > <ul class=\"nmcnav_primary nmcnav_ul\" aria-label=\"Primary Navigation\">. 60 menu items in total: 9 top level, 38 second level and 13 third level, 3 levels deep (only Work > Commercial / Institutional / Industrial reach level 3). Re-checked 2026-10-09 against https://claycorp.com/careers/ (HTTP 200, 136,703 bytes): the menu there is identical, except that the Careers <li> (menu-item-4954) carries the current-menu-item / current_page_item classes.",
    "Labels are verbatim, with HTML entities decoded: the source writes some ampersands as &#038; (Distribution & E-Commerce, Food & Beverage, Residential & Hospitality, Sports & Entertainment) and others as a literal & (Power & Energy, Systems & Equipment, VDC & BIM, Values & Commitments, Subcontractor & Vendor Resources). All render as \"&\".",
    "Items with children (Work, Commercial, Institutional, Industrial, Services, About Us, Contact, Building Solutions) are WordPress page menu items, but the site renders them as <button> toggles with aria-expanded/aria-controls and a .nav-dd-indicator span, with no href. Hence url \"\". The landing page for each group is the first child where one exists (Commercial > Featured Projects = /work/commercial, Institutional > Featured Projects = /work/institutional, Industrial > Featured Projects = /work/industrial, Services > Overview = /services). Work, About Us, Contact and Building Solutions have no 'overview' child.",
    "Header layout from the inline CSS: the hamburger nav toggle is order 1 (left), the Clayco logo order 2 (centre), and the search button order 3 (right). There is one menu for every width: the toggle has no desktop hide rule, and the panel (.nmcnav_panel) is a position:fixed drawer that is display:none until opened, then slides in from the left (nav-slidein, 0.3s ease-in-out). Submenus are nested in-panel dropdowns (class \"nmcnav_dropdown -standard\"), not a mega-menu. Header icons are white (#FFF) over the hero and switch to #212121 when .scrolled / .navopen / .header-color is set.",
    "Duplicate labels are real and intentional: \"Featured Projects\" appears 4 times (Work > Featured Projects = /work/featured-projects, plus the first child of Commercial, Institutional and Industrial). \"Sustainability\" appears twice (Services > Sustainability = /services/#sustainability and About Us > Sustainability = /claycos-sustainable-commitment).",
    "Label and slug mismatches to preserve exactly: Aviation -> /work/aerospace-aviation; Clayco Compute -> /work/mission-critical; Advanced Manufacturing -> /work/manufacturing; Distribution & E-Commerce -> /work/distribution; Life Sciences -> /work/life-science; Power & Energy -> /power-energy-storage (not under /work/); Sports & Entertainment sits under Work at top level but its URL is /work/commercial/sports-entertainment; Newsroom -> /latest; Contact > Offices -> /contact-us; Building Solutions > Integrated Approach -> /integrated-companies. Most Services children are anchors on /services/ (#preconstruction, #procurement, #construction, #design, #CDE, #SEI, #VDC, #TAG, #selfperform, #development, #sustainability). Anchor case is mixed as in source.",
    "External and new-tab behaviour: in the primary menu only the four Building Solutions company links (CRG https://realcrg.com/, LJC https://theljc.com/, Concrete Strategies https://concretestrategies.com/, Ventana https://ventana.vc/) are external, and all four carry target=\"_blank\" with no rel attribute. Every claycorp.com item opens in the same tab.",
    "menuLogos: inside the nav panel, after the primary <ul>, sits <div class=\"nmcnav_logos\"> holding two linked logo images, CRG (87px wide) then LJC (95px wide). Both use target=\"_blank\". The labels come from the img alt text.",
    "utility: the search button (title=\"Search\", data-nmc-micromodal-trigger=\"search-popup\") opens a modal rather than navigating. The url given is the resulting WordPress search query (GET https://claycorp.com?s=<term>). The 'menu' entry is the hamburger toggle's aria-label, not visible text.",
    "Footer: there is no footer <nav> or menu mirroring the primary navigation. Its blocks, in order, are: \"Offices\" (h2; 9 office cards with no links except tel: numbers: St. Louis, Chicago, South Carolina, Kansas City, Phoenix, Culver City, Birmingham, Atlanta, Raleigh); \"Building On Relationships\" (h2; 7 linked logos); \"Contact\" (h2; prose with inline links); the social icons; and the tertiary row (\"© 2026 Clayco\", the credits, and the legal <ul class=\"footer-legal_ul\">). The footer group labels \"Social\", \"Legal\" and \"Credits\" are descriptive names I added from class names. They are not visible text on the site.",
    "Footer logo labels are inferred from the image filenames because every footer logo img has alt=\"\". The footer LJC link (LJC-DE.png, max-width 180px) has no target=\"_blank\", unlike the other external logos. The Clayco SEI logo links internally to /services/#SEI. The Clayco logo links to https://claycorp.com/ with target=\"_blank\". Only the LJC, CRG, Concrete Strategies and Ventana footer links carry utm_source=claycorp.com&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=footer (in the HTML as &amp;, decoded here). The Clayco (https://claycorp.com/), Clayco SEI (https://claycorp.com/services/#SEI) and Clayco Rising (https://claycorising.com/) links have no UTM parameters.",
    "Footer Contact prose: the media, project, bid and prequalification email links are Cloudflare email-protected (/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#...). Their aria-labels show MediaInquiries@claycorp.com and info@claycorp.com. The bid and prequal addresses are obfuscated and were not recorded. The inline links Careers (target=\"_blank\") and \"Subcontractors or Vendors\" are recorded under footer > Contact.",
    "Social link labels: Instagram, Facebook and LinkedIn come from each icon's SVG <title>. The Twitter and YouTube SVGs have no <title>, so those two labels come from the class name (social__link--twitter / social__link--youtube) and the aria-label. The aria-labels are verbatim \"Follow  on Instagram\" etc., with a double space (the account name is missing in the template). All five open in a new tab."
  ]
}
